Usages:
  fan_in_boundary: |
    Roughly 16 distinct wire-format subpackages (promremotewrite, vmimport, csvimport, native,
    prometheusimport, influx, opentelemetry, zabbixconnector, newrelic, datadogv1, datadogv2,
    datadogsketches, graphite, opentsdb, opentsdbhttp) each parse their own protocol and convert
    it into the shared app/vminsert/common.InsertCtx API. Every path ends the same way:
    InsertCtx.FlushBufs() applies relabeling, runs stream aggregation, and commits rows through
    the storage entry point exposed by the storage-facing cell in this forest — in this pinned
    single-binary commit that entry point is an in-process call
    (vmstorage.VMInsertAPI.WriteRows), not a network RPC to separate storage-node processes.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the fan-in ingestion boundary of the system: whichever wire format a client uses
  to push metrics, this cell's `RequestHandler` routes the HTTP request to the matching
  subpackage, which normalizes it through common.InsertCtx and hands finished rows to the
  storage layer. Its own top-level exported functions carry no cross-cell-typed parameters (see
  this forest's Dependency Map for why no formal Imports are declared here), so its real
  dependencies on lib/promscrape (self-scrape ingestion) and the storage-facing cell are
  described here in prose rather than as DSL Imports.

  Use `fan_in_boundary` to understand the shape every new ingestion protocol handler must follow.

---

"Init()":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Wire up every ingestion subsystem this binary supports.

    Algorithm:
    1. Load the configured remote-write-style relabel config (own relabel subpackage) and
       initialize stream aggregation (common.InitStreamAggr)
    2. Initialize OpenTelemetry support and start a pool of parser worker goroutines
       (protoparserutil.StartUnmarshalWorkers)
    3. For each of the Graphite/Influx-line-protocol/OpenTSDB raw TCP/UDP listeners whose
       address flag is set, start it, wired to the matching subpackage's insert handler
    4. Start the self-scrape subsystem (promscrape), wired so scraped samples flow into the
       same push path as ingested rows
    5. Apply the configured per-series label-count/name-length/value-length limits

"Stop()":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Reverse of `Init`: stop the self-scrape subsystem, stop every running raw listener, stop the
    parser worker pool, and stop stream aggregation.

"RequestHandler(w: HTTPResponseWriter, r: HTTPRequest) -> handled:bool":
  location: main.go
  annotations: |
    Route one incoming HTTP request by URL path to the matching wire-format subpackage's insert
    handler, or to a promscrape control-plane endpoint (/targets, /config, /-/reload,
    readiness probe), returning false for unrecognized paths.

    Use `fan_in_boundary` for the full route-to-subpackage mapping and what happens after a
    subpackage accepts a request.

